## 8. Roles, Approvals & Segregation of Duties

| Role | Can do | Cannot do |
|---|---|---|
| Warehouse Staff (Receiver/Picker/Packer) | Scan receipts, pick, pack, dispatch | Post manual adjustments, edit cost/price |
| Warehouse Supervisor | Approve store requests within threshold, approve delivery variances within tolerance | Approve their own adjustments |
| Inventory Controller / Auditor | Post adjustments, run reconciliation, view full ledger, manage discrepancy cases | Approve adjustments they personally posted |
| Store Manager | Raise store requests, confirm store-side deliveries | Approve their own requests above auto-approve threshold |
| Sales Rep | Raise wholesale sales orders | Allocate inventory, approve credit exceptions |
| Approver / Ops Manager | Approve adjustments, returns-with-no-invoice, negative-stock overrides | Perform the underlying warehouse action being approved |
| Admin | Manage users, categories, master data | Bypass the ledger (no such capability exists for anyone) |

**Core rule (maker–checker):** the person who records a stock adjustment, scrap, or negative-stock override is never the person who approves it. This single rule closes the most common inventory-loss channel — one person with unilateral power to both create and justify a "correction."

